 0.2, 0.58, -0.6, -0.77, -1.04, -1.33]}}}, "built_at": "2026-08-07T13:35:40.216241+00:00"}, "be29efd84d19": {"label": "cross-asset \u00b7 2 series \u2191", "level": "amber", "score": 4.7, "members": ["usd_jpy", "dyn_amzn"], "articles": [{"title": "Global Market: Japan reveals record $40 billion yen-buying intervention as currency pressure persists", "feed": "ET Markets", "ts": "2026-08-07T05:23:57+00:00", "url": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/us-stocks/wall-street-guide/global-market-japan-reveals-record-40-billion-yen-buying-intervention-as-currency-pressure-persists/articleshow/133021238.cms", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "Japan carried out its largest-ever single-day currency intervention, deploying nearly $40 billion to support the yen amid sharp depreciation. Detailed data from the Ministry of Finance showed authorities intervened multiple times during the Golden Week holidays, while markets remain alert for further action as the yen weakens again.\n\n(What's moving Sensex and Nifty Track latest market news, stock tips, Budget 2025, Share Market on Budget 2025 and expert advice, on ETMarkets. Also, ETMarkets.com is now on Telegram. For fastest news alerts on financial markets, investment strategies and stocks alerts, subscribe to our Telegram feeds .)\n\nSubscribe to ET Prime and read the Economic Times ePaper ", "citation": "Global Market: Japan reveals record $40 billion yen-buying intervention as currency pressure persists \u2014 ET Markets, 2026-08-07. https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/us-stocks/wall-street-guide/global-market-japan-reveals-record-40-billion-yen-buying-intervention-as-currency-pressure-persists/articleshow/133021238.cms"}, {"title": "Yen Surrenders Nearly Half Its Gains from US-Japan Intervention", "feed": "Mint Markets", "ts": "2026-08-07T00:24:08+00:00", "url": "https://www.livemint.com/market/yen-surrenders-nearly-half-its-gains-from-us-japan-intervention-11786062248662.html", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "The yen is heading into the end of the week having surrendered nearly half of its intervention-driven gains, fueling speculation among traders that authorities may step into the market again.\n\nThe currency traded around 158.45 versus the dollar on Friday morning, well off the strong point of 155.23 reached on Monday. It had been near a four-decade nadir around 164 per dollar last week before the first joint yen-buying operation from Japan and the US since 1998.\n\nThe pullback underscores the limits of intervention in reversing the yen\u2019s longer-term decline, with a wide interest-rate gap to the US, Japan\u2019s high debt load and geopolitical uncertainty continuing to weigh on the currency. Meanwhi", "citation": "Yen Surrenders Nearly Half Its Gains from US-Japan Intervention \u2014 Mint Markets, 2026-08-07. https://www.livemint.com/market/yen-surrenders-nearly-half-its-gains-from-us-japan-intervention-11786062248662.html"}, {"title": "Japan Carmakers See Yen Remaining Near Post-Intervention Levels", "feed": "Mint Markets", "ts": "2026-08-06T21:21:41+00:00", "url": "https://www.livemint.com/market/japan-carmakers-see-yen-remaining-near-post-intervention-levels-11786051302266.html", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "Japan\u2019s carmakers are assuming that the yen will trade near current levels against the US dollar in the coming months, based on forecasts they issued just as the US stepped in to help the Japanese currency from weakening further.\n\nToyota Motor Corp., Nissan Motor Co. and others based their profit and sales outlooks on the view that the currency will remain at \u00a5150 to \u00a5160 against the dollar for the fiscal year through March 2027, according to their latest round of results. The yen is currently trading within that range, at around \u00a5157.7 as of Thursday.\n\nOver the past week, the governments of the US and Japan took joint action in the currency markets for the first time since 2011, seeking to ", "citation": "Japan Carmakers See Yen Remaining Near Post-Intervention Levels \u2014 Mint Markets, 2026-08-06. https://www.livemint.com/market/japan-carmakers-see-yen-remaining-near-post-intervention-levels-11786051302266.html"}], "primary_sources": [{"series": "usd_jpy", "name": "Yahoo \u00b7 JPY=X", "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JPY=X"}, {"series": "dyn_amzn", "name": "Yahoo \u00b7 AMZN", "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AMZN"}], "analogues": {"member_z_today": {"usd_jpy": 1.1, "dyn_amzn": -0.15}, "analogues": [{"date": "2024-10-16", "distance": 0.15, "member_z": {"usd_jpy": 1.31, "dyn_amzn": -0.19}}, {"date": "2024-11-21", "distance": 0.23, "member_z": {"usd_jpy": 1.42, "dyn_amzn": -0.21}}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "distance": 0.24, "member_z": {"usd_jpy": 1.33, "dyn_amzn": -0.4}}, {"date": "2025-10-22", "distance": 0.25, "member_z": {"usd_jpy": 0.96, "dyn_amzn": -0.48}}, {"date": "2026-05-22", "distance": 0.27, "member_z": {"usd_jpy": 0.72, "dyn_amzn": -0.15}}], "aftermath": {"usd_jpy": {"stats": {"+5d": {"n": 5, "median_pct": -0.1, "hit_rate_up": 0.4, "min_pct": -2.55, "max_pct": 1.37}, "+20d": {"n": 5, "median_pct": 1.43, "hit_rate_up": 0.6, "min_pct": -1.11, "max_pct": 3.73}}, "median_path": [0.0, -0.05, -0.04, 0.14, 0.35, -0.1, 0.21, 0.39, 0.6, 0.58, 0.61, 0.82, 0.69, 0.86, 0.95, 0.7, 0.59, 0.76, 0.88, 0.99]}, "dyn_amzn": {"stats": {"+5d": {"n": 4, "median_pct": 2.13, "hit_rate_up": 0.75, "min_pct": -1.17, "max_pct": 5.67}, "+20d": {"n": 4, "median_pct": 12.86, "hit_rate_up": 1.0, "min_pct": 2.11, "max_pct": 24.69}}, "median_path": [0.0, 0.34, 1.55, 2.88, 2.64, 4.79, 2.25, 7.59, 9.97, 11.18, 14.44, 11.51, 12.14, 13.97, 14.29, 12.04, 12.39, 11.39, 10.67]}, "sp500": {"stats": {"+5d": {"n": 4, "median_pct": 1.39, "hit_rate_up": 0.75, "min_pct": -0.77, "max_pct": 2.85}, "+20d": {"n": 4, "median_pct": 0.61, "hit_rate_up": 0.5, "min_pct": -1.29, "max_pct": 9.35}}, "median_path": [0.0, 0.58, 0.65, 1.23, 1.35, 1.69, 1.82, 1.7, 2.28, 1.08, 1.45, 0.31, 0.44, 1.99, 1.72, 1.72, 2.11, 1.71, 0.36]}, "hy